.TH "HEE-INDEX" "1" "" "" "HEE Tools"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
hee-index - generate hee/INDEX.md, the persisted index of every HEE
object
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
hee-index [--out FILE]
hee-index help
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
Walks every HEE object (apiVersion: hee/v1) in the current repo, groups
them by kind, and writes an index carrying each object\[aq]s live pass/fail
compliance status.

A thin wrapper around hee-lint\[aq]s own scan -- it reuses that pass/fail
logic rather than parsing YAML a second time, so there is one
implementation of \[dq]is this object valid\[dq], not two.

  --out   where to write the index. Default: hee/INDEX.md

The output is generated state and is checked for staleness in CI; run
this and commit the result whenever objects change.
\f[R]
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
0 written   1 unknown argument   2 not in a git repo
\f[R]
.fi
